From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: count the fast path on the interfaces it skips

The fast path receives a flow on the device under a bridge, VLAN or PPP
interface and transmits on that device directly, so the statistics of
the interfaces above it stop moving for every offloaded flow: a router
with the flowtable on its switch ports shows megabytes on br-lan for
gigabytes on wan.

Record the interfaces above the ingress device from the forward path
and update their counters from the fast path: on receive with the
packet as the interface would have delivered it, on transmit with the
frame as sent, down to the device the frame is handed to, which counts
for itself from there on. The bridge and ppp keep their statistics in
the per-cpu tstats, a VLAN interface in its own per-cpu block.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
